From 0ddbfa5cce820cdc1785392a5714426a5bf156a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:24:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Stadium transformations: no field in the public match
 config, no environment switch

The field sat in MslMatchConfig's trailing padding, so a driver built on the
base's layout, or one that does not zero the struct, turned transformations
on (or was refused) for every match. The public API, its Python dtype and
MatchConfig are the base's again, and MSL_STADIUM_TRANSFORMATIONS is gone:
only a suite entry's "stadium_transformations": true or
--stadium-transformations turns them on. replay-bench loads GameData with
the option only for tapes built with it.

stadium-defaults-smoke (no game data) builds configs as the base's drivers
do, over noise, for non-Stadium and Stadium replays, and checks the setting
stays off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017JX71xgnBPBiwucag1mFRr
